#  16-bit compact instruction decode.
#
#  This file is generated/hand-written separately; see README.md, "Compact
#  16-bit fetch packets", for the model and for the current coverage.
#
#  STATUS: work in progress.  The framework side is complete - the compact
#  fetch-packet header is decoded (CPKT, see c6000_manual.sinc), the header
#  parameters are folded into the decode context by c6000.C6000PacketContext,
#  and c6000_manual.sinc provides a two-byte UNKNOWN16 fallback so that linear
#  sweeps stay synchronised through compact packets.  The per-opcode
#  constructors for the sixteen-bit maps (SPRUFE8B appendices C.4, D.4, E.4,
#  F.4, G.3 and H.4) are not yet enabled: they still need their table
#  definitions completed before the SLEIGH compiler accepts them.
#
#  Until they land, a compact slot decodes as the correctly-sized two-byte
#  UNKNOWN16 placeholder, so instruction boundaries, packet boundaries and
#  everything after a compact packet remain correct; only the mnemonic and
#  semantics of the compact instruction itself are missing.  The corpus test
#  reports that count per image.
